window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b128-72f418dac0f672e3.json"]={sha256:"72f418dac0f672e38f00af98481d0f096fbc6eae5276b4a8050b0d17282be1e2",value:{"id":"b128","title":"鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類","titleEn":"Core logging and rock-mass classification","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦從回次、節理與試驗代表性推導岩體分類的適用邊界。沿著調查依據、物理作用、數量估算、現場驗證到工程交接逐項建立可追溯的推論鏈，特別辨別單一數值無法揭露的空間差異及時間效應。以獨立量測檢驗簡化模型，並把觀測結果、教學假設與需要主管工程師審查的決策清楚分列。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on derive rock-mass classification boundaries from runs, discontinuities and test representativeness. It develops a traceable reasoning chain from evidence and physical processes through quantitative estimates, field verification and engineering handover. Spatial variation and time effects are separated from a single nominal result. Independent observations test the simplified models, while measured evidence, teaching assumptions and decisions requiring the responsible engineer remain explicitly distinguished.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-investigation","subcategoryTitle":"地質調查與變形監測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Ground investigation and deformation monitoring","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-investigation","learningTags":["underground","ug-investigation","survey"],"architectureFamily":"survey","architectureNodes":[["回次與深度閉合","Runs and depth closure"],["節理間距方向","Directional joint spacing"],["單軸強度與取樣","Uniaxial strength and sampling"],["乘法指標敏感","Multiplicative index sensitivity"],["分類到模型交接","Classification-to-model handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[3,1]],"diagram":{"type":"survey","labels":["回次與深度閉合","節理間距方向","單軸強度與取樣","乘法指標敏感","分類到模型交接"],"labelsEn":["Runs and depth closure","Directional joint spacing","Uniaxial strength and sampling","Multiplicative index sensitivity","Classification-to-model handover"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學算例，所有輸入是為比較機制而假設，並非任何地標的實測資料。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設鑽進3.0 m、岩心2.7 m，TCR=90%，缺失0.3 m；缺失所在深度仍不唯一。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設2 m回次內長度至少100 mm的健全岩心合計1.4 m，RQD=1.4/2×100=70%。將第一式的一個線性乘數加倍而固定其他邊界，該項貢獻隨之加倍；若為非線性式則必須重新代入，不能等比例外推。把輸入值、單位換算、計算結果及假設列成四欄，再用獨立計算器重算；最後比較量測誤差與模型簡化，判斷改變是否足以支持工程決策。","textEn":"Original teaching example: all inputs are assumptions for comparing mechanisms, not measurements from a landmark project. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed advance 3.0 m and recovered core 2.7 m, TCR=90% and loss=0.3 m; the location of that loss remains nonunique. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If sound pieces at least 100 mm long total an assumed 1.4 m within a 2 m run, RQD=1.4/2×100=70%. Doubling one linear multiplicative input in the first relation while holding the remaining boundaries fixed doubles that contribution; a nonlinear relation must instead be evaluated again. Tabulate inputs, unit conversions, results and assumptions in separate columns, and recalculate independently. Finally compare measurement uncertainty with model simplification before deciding whether the difference supports an engineering decision.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b128-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「回次與深度閉合」與「岩石品質指標」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Runs and depth closure\" and \"Rock quality designation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b128-v14-01","title":"回次與深度閉合：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Runs and depth closure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「回次與深度閉合」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Runs and depth closure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岩心箱的順序建立地下空間的索引，鑽進回次與回收長度不閉合時，後續試驗再精準也會失去位置。接桿量測、殘留岩心與鑽具長度須分開記錄，不能把深度誤差藏入某個破碎段。 假設鑽進3.0 m、岩心2.7 m，TCR=90%，缺失0.3 m；缺失所在深度仍不唯一。 把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回次與深度閉合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Core-box order indexes subsurface space. If advance and recovery do not close, even precise tests lose their location. Record rod measurements, retained core and tooling lengths separately instead of hiding a depth discrepancy inside a broken interval. For assumed advance 3.0 m and recovered core 2.7 m, TCR=90% and loss=0.3 m; the location of that loss remains nonunique. Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material. A smooth subsequent strength profile then represents the wrong depths. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Runs and depth closure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回次與深度閉合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Runs and depth closure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-01-k1","title":"回次與深度閉合","titleEn":"Runs and depth closure","text":"岩心箱的順序建立地下空間的索引，鑽進回次與回收長度不閉合時，後續試驗再精準也會失去位置。接桿量測、殘留岩心與鑽具長度須分開記錄，不能把深度誤差藏入某個破碎段。","textEn":"Core-box order indexes subsurface space. If advance and recovery do not close, even precise tests lose their location.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回次與深度閉合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Runs and depth closure\" is correct?","options":["岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。","岩心箱的順序建立地下空間的索引，鑽進回次與回收長度不閉合時，後續試驗再精準也會失去位置。","岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。"],"optionsEn":["Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run.","Core-box order indexes subsurface space.","High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"岩心箱的順序建立地下空間的索引，鑽進回次與回收長度不閉合時，後續試驗再精準也會失去位置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Core-box order indexes subsurface space. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b128-v14-02","title":"回次與深度閉合：定量估算","titleEn":"Runs and depth closure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回次與深度閉合」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Runs and depth closure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設鑽進3.0 m、岩心2.7 m，TCR=90%，缺失0.3 m；缺失所在深度仍不唯一。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed advance 3.0 m and recovered core 2.7 m, TCR=90% and loss=0.3 m; the location of that loss remains nonunique. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對鑽班原始進尺、岩心箱分隔牌與完整照片，重新量測岩心長度；深度無法閉合的回次需標出不確定區間，待記錄者與地質師共同釐清，不能默默移動標牌。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile original drilling advance, run dividers and complete photographs and remeasure recovered length; mark unresolved intervals for joint review by the logger and geologist rather than silently moving a divider.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設鑽進3.0 m、岩心2.7 m，TCR=90%，缺失0.3 m；缺失所在深度仍不唯一。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed advance 3.0 m and recovered core 2.7 m, TCR=90% and loss=0.3 m; the location of that loss remains nonunique.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回次與深度閉合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Runs and depth closure\", which statement holds?","options":["洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。","岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior.","Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b128-v14-03","title":"回次與深度閉合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Runs and depth closure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回次與深度閉合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Runs and depth closure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對鑽班原始進尺、岩心箱分隔牌與完整照片，重新量測岩心長度；深度無法閉合的回次需標出不確定區間，待記錄者與地質師共同釐清，不能默默移動標牌。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile original drilling advance, run dividers and complete photographs and remeasure recovered length; mark unresolved intervals for joint review by the logger and geologist rather than silently moving a divider. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material. A smooth subsequent strength profile then represents the wrong depths. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄回次與深度閉合的資料來源與適用條件。核對鑽班原始進尺、岩心箱分隔牌與完整照片，重新量測岩心長度；深度無法閉合的回次需標出不確定區間，待記錄者與地質師共同釐清，不能默默移動標牌。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for runs and depth closure. Reconcile original drilling advance, run dividers and complete photographs and remeasure recovered length; mark unresolved intervals for joint review by the logger and geologist rather than silently moving a divider.","failure":"注意干擾：把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對鑽班原始進尺、岩心箱分隔牌與完整照片，重新量測岩心長度；深度無法閉合的回次需標出不確定區間，待記錄者與地質師共同釐清，不能默默移動標牌。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。","textEn":"Reconcile original drilling advance, run dividers and complete photographs and remeasure recovered length; mark unresolved intervals for joint review by the logger and geologist rather than silently moving a divider. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material. A smooth subsequent strength profile then represents the wrong depths.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄回次與深度閉合的資料來源與適用條件。核對鑽班原始進尺、岩心箱分隔牌與完整照片，重新量測岩心長度；深度無法閉合的回次需標出不確定區間，待記錄者與地質師共同釐清，不能默默移動標牌。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for runs and depth closure. Reconcile original drilling advance, run dividers and complete photographs and remeasure recovered length; mark unresolved intervals for joint review by the logger and geologist rather than silently moving a divider.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回次與深度閉合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Runs and depth closure\"?","options":["核對鑽班原始進尺、岩心箱分隔牌與完整照片，重新量測岩心長度；深度無法閉合的回次需標出不確定區間，待記錄者與地質師共同釐清，不能默默移動標牌。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile original drilling advance, run dividers and complete photographs and remeasure recovered length.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對鑽班原始進尺、岩心箱分隔牌與完整照片，重新量測岩心長度；深度無法閉合的回次需標出不確定區間，待記錄者與地質師共同釐清，不能默默移動標牌。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile original drilling advance, run dividers and complete photographs and remeasure recovered length; mark unresolved intervals for joint review by the logger and geologist rather than silently moving a divider. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b128-v14-04","title":"回次與深度閉合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Runs and depth closure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回次與深度閉合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Runs and depth closure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material. A smooth subsequent strength profile then represents the wrong depths. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A smooth subsequent strength profile then represents the wrong depths.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。","textEn":"Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material. A smooth subsequent strength profile then represents the wrong depths.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回次與深度閉合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Runs and depth closure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。","岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material.","High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把孔底殘留岩心歸入下一回次會重複或錯置地層，缺失區則可能被假想成完整材料；其後的強度曲線雖連續，卻不對應真實深度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning retained bottom core to the next run duplicates or shifts geology and can fill losses with imaginary intact material. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b128-v14-05","title":"岩石品質指標：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rock quality designation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「岩石品質指標」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rock quality designation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"RQD只計符合長度條件的健全岩心，機械折斷應辨識並重接；它反映沿孔方向的塊體分割，而不是完整三維岩體強度。與孔平行的節理很少被截交，方向偏差必須保留。 假設2 m回次內長度至少100 mm的健全岩心合計1.4 m，RQD=1.4/2×100=70%。 把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岩石品質指標」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"RQD counts sound pieces meeting a length criterion, with recognized mechanical breaks reassembled. It describes segmentation along the hole rather than three-dimensional mass strength. Joints parallel to the hole are undersampled, so directional bias remains. If sound pieces at least 100 mm long total an assumed 1.4 m within a 2 m run, RQD=1.4/2×100=70%. Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD. Conversely, high RQD can coexist with one persistent plane controlling a large wedge, so support demand is not determined by that percentage alone. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rock quality designation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岩石品質指標」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rock quality designation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-05-k1","title":"岩石品質指標","titleEn":"Rock quality designation","text":"RQD只計符合長度條件的健全岩心，機械折斷應辨識並重接；它反映沿孔方向的塊體分割，而不是完整三維岩體強度。與孔平行的節理很少被截交，方向偏差必須保留。","textEn":"RQD counts sound pieces meeting a length criterion, with recognized mechanical breaks reassembled. It describes segmentation along the hole rather than three-dimensional mass strength.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岩石品質指標」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rock quality designation\" is correct?","options":["岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。","不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。","RQD只計符合長度條件的健全岩心，機械折斷應辨識並重接；它反映沿孔方向的塊體分割，而不是完整三維岩體強度。"],"optionsEn":["High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation.","Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction.","RQD counts sound pieces meeting a length criterion, with recognized mechanical breaks reassembled."],"answer":2,"explanation":"RQD只計符合長度條件的健全岩心，機械折斷應辨識並重接；它反映沿孔方向的塊體分割，而不是完整三維岩體強度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"RQD counts sound pieces meeting a length criterion, with recognized mechanical breaks reassembled. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b128-v14-06","title":"岩石品質指標：定量估算","titleEn":"Rock quality designation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岩石品質指標」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rock quality designation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設2 m回次內長度至少100 mm的健全岩心合計1.4 m，RQD=1.4/2×100=70%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If sound pieces at least 100 mm long total an assumed 1.4 m within a 2 m run, RQD=1.4/2×100=70%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用端面吻合與新鮮破面區分機械斷裂，逐段保留計入長度及照片；另一位記錄者獨立複核臨界長度岩心，再對照孔方向與節理組，確認分類未忽略取樣方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Distinguish mechanical breaks using matching fresh ends and retain counted lengths and photographs; a second logger checks borderline pieces, then compares hole orientation with joint sets to expose directional sampling bias.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設2 m回次內長度至少100 mm的健全岩心合計1.4 m，RQD=1.4/2×100=70%。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If sound pieces at least 100 mm long total an assumed 1.4 m within a 2 m run, RQD=1.4/2×100=70%.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岩石品質指標」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rock quality designation\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。","乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass.","The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b128-v14-07","title":"岩石品質指標：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rock quality designation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岩石品質指標」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rock quality designation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用端面吻合與新鮮破面區分機械斷裂，逐段保留計入長度及照片；另一位記錄者獨立複核臨界長度岩心，再對照孔方向與節理組，確認分類未忽略取樣方向。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Distinguish mechanical breaks using matching fresh ends and retain counted lengths and photographs; a second logger checks borderline pieces, then compares hole orientation with joint sets to expose directional sampling bias. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD. Conversely, high RQD can coexist with one persistent plane controlling a large wedge, so support demand is not determined by that percentage alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄岩石品質指標的資料來源與適用條件。用端面吻合與新鮮破面區分機械斷裂，逐段保留計入長度及照片；另一位記錄者獨立複核臨界長度岩心，再對照孔方向與節理組，確認分類未忽略取樣方向。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for rock quality designation. Distinguish mechanical breaks using matching fresh ends and retain counted lengths and photographs; a second logger checks borderline pieces, then compares hole orientation with joint sets to expose directional sampling bias.","failure":"注意干擾：把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用端面吻合與新鮮破面區分機械斷裂，逐段保留計入長度及照片；另一位記錄者獨立複核臨界長度岩心，再對照孔方向與節理組，確認分類未忽略取樣方向。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。","textEn":"Distinguish mechanical breaks using matching fresh ends and retain counted lengths and photographs; a second logger checks borderline pieces, then compares hole orientation with joint sets to expose directional sampling bias. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD. Conversely, high RQD can coexist with one persistent plane controlling a large wedge, so support demand is not determined by that percentage alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄岩石品質指標的資料來源與適用條件。用端面吻合與新鮮破面區分機械斷裂，逐段保留計入長度及照片；另一位記錄者獨立複核臨界長度岩心，再對照孔方向與節理組，確認分類未忽略取樣方向。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for rock quality designation. Distinguish mechanical breaks using matching fresh ends and retain counted lengths and photographs; a second logger checks borderline pieces, then compares hole orientation with joint sets to expose directional sampling bias.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岩石品質指標」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rock quality designation\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用端面吻合與新鮮破面區分機械斷裂，逐段保留計入長度及照片；另一位記錄者獨立複核臨界長度岩心，再對照孔方向與節理組，確認分類未忽略取樣方向。","兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Distinguish mechanical breaks using matching fresh ends and retain counted lengths and photographs.","Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用端面吻合與新鮮破面區分機械斷裂，逐段保留計入長度及照片；另一位記錄者獨立複核臨界長度岩心，再對照孔方向與節理組，確認分類未忽略取樣方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Distinguish mechanical breaks using matching fresh ends and retain counted lengths and photographs; a second logger checks borderline pieces, then compares hole orientation with joint sets to expose directional sampling bias. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b128-v14-08","title":"岩石品質指標：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rock quality designation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岩石品質指標」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rock quality designation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD. Conversely, high RQD can coexist with one persistent plane controlling a large wedge, so support demand is not determined by that percentage alone. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Conversely, high RQD can coexist with one persistent plane controlling a large wedge, so support demand is not determined by that percentage alone.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。","textEn":"Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD. Conversely, high RQD can coexist with one persistent plane controlling a large wedge, so support demand is not determined by that percentage alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岩石品質指標」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rock quality designation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。","把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction.","Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把鑽具造成的折斷當成自然節理會低估RQD；只看高RQD又可能漏掉一條控制大楔體的持續節理，支護需求並不隨單一百分比單調決定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting drilling breaks as natural joints underestimates RQD. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b128-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「節理間距方向」與「節理表面與充填」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Directional joint spacing\" and \"Joint surfaces and infill\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b128-v14-09","title":"節理間距方向：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Directional joint spacing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「節理間距方向」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Directional joint spacing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"掃描線截交頻率取決於節理法線和測線夾角；同一岩體由不同方向鑽孔會得到不同表觀間距。幾何修正接近平行時變得不穩定，應報告不可辨識的組別而非無限放大權重。 假設真法向間距0.3 m、測線與法線60°，表觀間距0.3/cos60°=0.6 m。 忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「節理間距方向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Intersection frequency depends on the angle between joint normal and survey line. Different hole directions produce different apparent spacing. Corrections become unstable near parallel orientation, requiring an unresolved-set warning rather than unbounded weighting. Assume normal spacing 0.3 m and a 60° angle between line and normal; apparent spacing is 0.3/cos60°=0.6 m. Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size. Aggressive correction of a few intersections can instead let one observation dominate the statistics. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Directional joint spacing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「節理間距方向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Directional joint spacing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-09-k1","title":"節理間距方向","titleEn":"Directional joint spacing","text":"掃描線截交頻率取決於節理法線和測線夾角；同一岩體由不同方向鑽孔會得到不同表觀間距。幾何修正接近平行時變得不穩定，應報告不可辨識的組別而非無限放大權重。","textEn":"Intersection frequency depends on the angle between joint normal and survey line. Different hole directions produce different apparent spacing.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「節理間距方向」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Directional joint spacing\" is correct?","options":["掃描線截交頻率取決於節理法線和測線夾角；同一岩體由不同方向鑽孔會得到不同表觀間距。","不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。","洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。"],"optionsEn":["Intersection frequency depends on the angle between joint normal and survey line.","Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction.","Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"掃描線截交頻率取決於節理法線和測線夾角；同一岩體由不同方向鑽孔會得到不同表觀間距。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Intersection frequency depends on the angle between joint normal and survey line. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b128-v14-10","title":"節理間距方向：定量估算","titleEn":"Directional joint spacing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「節理間距方向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Directional joint spacing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設真法向間距0.3 m、測線與法線60°，表觀間距0.3/cos60°=0.6 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume normal spacing 0.3 m and a 60° angle between line and normal; apparent spacing is 0.3/cos60°=0.6 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將孔軸與節理極點畫在同一球面投影，查核取向資料的定向基準；以不同方向孔或露頭掃描線交叉驗證，接近平行且樣本稀少的組別須在報告中明示下限或缺口。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot hole axes and joint poles on the same stereonet and verify orientation datum; cross-check differently directed holes or exposure scanlines and state bounds or gaps for nearly parallel, sparsely sampled sets.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設真法向間距0.3 m、測線與法線60°，表觀間距0.3/cos60°=0.6 m。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume normal spacing 0.3 m and a 60° angle between line and normal; apparent spacing is 0.3/cos60°=0.6 m.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「節理間距方向」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Directional joint spacing\", which statement holds?","options":["岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b128-v14-11","title":"節理間距方向：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Directional joint spacing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「節理間距方向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Directional joint spacing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將孔軸與節理極點畫在同一球面投影，查核取向資料的定向基準；以不同方向孔或露頭掃描線交叉驗證，接近平行且樣本稀少的組別須在報告中明示下限或缺口。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot hole axes and joint poles on the same stereonet and verify orientation datum; cross-check differently directed holes or exposure scanlines and state bounds or gaps for nearly parallel, sparsely sampled sets. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size. Aggressive correction of a few intersections can instead let one observation dominate the statistics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄節理間距方向的資料來源與適用條件。將孔軸與節理極點畫在同一球面投影，查核取向資料的定向基準；以不同方向孔或露頭掃描線交叉驗證，接近平行且樣本稀少的組別須在報告中明示下限或缺口。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for directional joint spacing. Plot hole axes and joint poles on the same stereonet and verify orientation datum; cross-check differently directed holes or exposure scanlines and state bounds or gaps for nearly parallel, sparsely sampled sets.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將孔軸與節理極點畫在同一球面投影，查核取向資料的定向基準；以不同方向孔或露頭掃描線交叉驗證，接近平行且樣本稀少的組別須在報告中明示下限或缺口。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。","textEn":"Plot hole axes and joint poles on the same stereonet and verify orientation datum; cross-check differently directed holes or exposure scanlines and state bounds or gaps for nearly parallel, sparsely sampled sets. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size. Aggressive correction of a few intersections can instead let one observation dominate the statistics.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄節理間距方向的資料來源與適用條件。將孔軸與節理極點畫在同一球面投影，查核取向資料的定向基準；以不同方向孔或露頭掃描線交叉驗證，接近平行且樣本稀少的組別須在報告中明示下限或缺口。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for directional joint spacing. Plot hole axes and joint poles on the same stereonet and verify orientation datum; cross-check differently directed holes or exposure scanlines and state bounds or gaps for nearly parallel, sparsely sampled sets.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「節理間距方向」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Directional joint spacing\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。","將孔軸與節理極點畫在同一球面投影，查核取向資料的定向基準；以不同方向孔或露頭掃描線交叉驗證，接近平行且樣本稀少的組別須在報告中明示下限或缺口。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage.","Plot hole axes and joint poles on the same stereonet and verify orientation datum."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將孔軸與節理極點畫在同一球面投影，查核取向資料的定向基準；以不同方向孔或露頭掃描線交叉驗證，接近平行且樣本稀少的組別須在報告中明示下限或缺口。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot hole axes and joint poles on the same stereonet and verify orientation datum; cross-check differently directed holes or exposure scanlines and state bounds or gaps for nearly parallel, sparsely sampled sets. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b128-v14-12","title":"節理間距方向：失效診斷","titleEn":"Directional joint spacing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「節理間距方向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Directional joint spacing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size. Aggressive correction of a few intersections can instead let one observation dominate the statistics. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Aggressive correction of a few intersections can instead let one observation dominate the statistics.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。","textEn":"Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size. Aggressive correction of a few intersections can instead let one observation dominate the statistics.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「節理間距方向」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Directional joint spacing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略方向會把一組密集但與孔平行的節理判成稀疏，造成塊體尺寸高估；粗暴修正少數截交又會讓單一節理主導整體統計。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring orientation makes a closely spaced, hole-parallel joint set appear sparse and overestimates block size. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b128-v14-13","title":"節理表面與充填：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint surfaces and infill: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「節理表面與充填」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint surfaces and infill” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節理粗糙度、風化與充填共同決定剪力機制，兩個表面是否接觸比單看顏色重要。厚軟填土可隔開岩壁粗糙峰，於是完整岩石強度再高也不能代表節理面的抗剪能力。 假設填料厚4 mm、有效粗糙峰高2 mm，厚度比4/2=2；此幾何比不等於可直接使用的強度折減係數。 洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「節理表面與充填」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Roughness, weathering and infill jointly govern joint shear. Contact between opposing walls matters more than color. Thick weak infill can separate rough rock asperities, making intact rock strength irrelevant to the shearing plane. For assumed infill thickness 4 mm and effective asperity height 2 mm, the ratio is 2; this geometric ratio is not a directly usable strength-reduction factor. Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening. An apparently favorable joint can still slide after excavation unloading and seepage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint surfaces and infill” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「節理表面與充填」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint surfaces and infill”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-13-k1","title":"節理表面與充填","titleEn":"Joint surfaces and infill","text":"節理粗糙度、風化與充填共同決定剪力機制，兩個表面是否接觸比單看顏色重要。厚軟填土可隔開岩壁粗糙峰，於是完整岩石強度再高也不能代表節理面的抗剪能力。","textEn":"Roughness, weathering and infill jointly govern joint shear. Contact between opposing walls matters more than color.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「節理表面與充填」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint surfaces and infill\" is correct?","options":["洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。","節理粗糙度、風化與充填共同決定剪力機制，兩個表面是否接觸比單看顏色重要。","完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。"],"optionsEn":["Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior.","Roughness, weathering and infill jointly govern joint shear.","Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"節理粗糙度、風化與充填共同決定剪力機制，兩個表面是否接觸比單看顏色重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Roughness, weathering and infill jointly govern joint shear. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b128-v14-14","title":"節理表面與充填：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint surfaces and infill: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「節理表面與充填」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint surfaces and infill” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設填料厚4 mm、有效粗糙峰高2 mm，厚度比4/2=2；此幾何比不等於可直接使用的強度折減係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed infill thickness 4 mm and effective asperity height 2 mm, the ratio is 2; this geometric ratio is not a directly usable strength-reduction factor. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以比例照片、觸感及樣品描述保存填料厚度和連續性，避免清洗後才記錄；同時比較飽和狀態及相同法向應力的剪力試驗，只有一致的材料與邊界條件才可互相比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Preserve scaled photographs and samples of infill thickness and continuity before washing; compare saturation and shear tests at matching normal stress, accepting comparisons only for consistent material and boundary conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設填料厚4 mm、有效粗糙峰高2 mm，厚度比4/2=2；此幾何比不等於可直接使用的強度折減係數。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed infill thickness 4 mm and effective asperity height 2 mm, the ratio is 2; this geometric ratio is not a directly usable strength-reduction factor.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「節理表面與充填」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint surfaces and infill\", which statement holds?","options":["乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。","兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction.","Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b128-v14-15","title":"節理表面與充填：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint surfaces and infill: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「節理表面與充填」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint surfaces and infill” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以比例照片、觸感及樣品描述保存填料厚度和連續性，避免清洗後才記錄；同時比較飽和狀態及相同法向應力的剪力試驗，只有一致的材料與邊界條件才可互相比對。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Preserve scaled photographs and samples of infill thickness and continuity before washing; compare saturation and shear tests at matching normal stress, accepting comparisons only for consistent material and boundary conditions. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening. An apparently favorable joint can still slide after excavation unloading and seepage. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄節理表面與充填的資料來源與適用條件。以比例照片、觸感及樣品描述保存填料厚度和連續性，避免清洗後才記錄；同時比較飽和狀態及相同法向應力的剪力試驗，只有一致的材料與邊界條件才可互相比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for joint surfaces and infill. Preserve scaled photographs and samples of infill thickness and continuity before washing; compare saturation and shear tests at matching normal stress, accepting comparisons only for consistent material and boundary conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以比例照片、觸感及樣品描述保存填料厚度和連續性，避免清洗後才記錄；同時比較飽和狀態及相同法向應力的剪力試驗，只有一致的材料與邊界條件才可互相比對。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。","textEn":"Preserve scaled photographs and samples of infill thickness and continuity before washing; compare saturation and shear tests at matching normal stress, accepting comparisons only for consistent material and boundary conditions. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening. An apparently favorable joint can still slide after excavation unloading and seepage.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄節理表面與充填的資料來源與適用條件。以比例照片、觸感及樣品描述保存填料厚度和連續性，避免清洗後才記錄；同時比較飽和狀態及相同法向應力的剪力試驗，只有一致的材料與邊界條件才可互相比對。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for joint surfaces and infill. Preserve scaled photographs and samples of infill thickness and continuity before washing; compare saturation and shear tests at matching normal stress, accepting comparisons only for consistent material and boundary conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「節理表面與充填」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint surfaces and infill\"?","options":["以比例照片、觸感及樣品描述保存填料厚度和連續性，避免清洗後才記錄；同時比較飽和狀態及相同法向應力的剪力試驗，只有一致的材料與邊界條件才可互相比對。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。"],"optionsEn":["Preserve scaled photographs and samples of infill thickness and continuity before washing.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以比例照片、觸感及樣品描述保存填料厚度和連續性，避免清洗後才記錄；同時比較飽和狀態及相同法向應力的剪力試驗，只有一致的材料與邊界條件才可互相比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Preserve scaled photographs and samples of infill thickness and continuity before washing; compare saturation and shear tests at matching normal stress, accepting comparisons only for consistent material and boundary conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b128-v14-16","title":"節理表面與充填：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint surfaces and infill: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「節理表面與充填」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint surfaces and infill” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening. An apparently favorable joint can still slide after excavation unloading and seepage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An apparently favorable joint can still slide after excavation unloading and seepage.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。","textEn":"Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening. An apparently favorable joint can still slide after excavation unloading and seepage.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「節理表面與充填」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint surfaces and infill\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。","完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening.","Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"洗去黏土後記錄的粗糙岩壁會誇大現地摩擦力，乾燥樣品也可能掩蓋遇水軟化；看似良好節理在開挖卸荷與滲水後仍可能滑動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Washing clay away exaggerates the friction represented by rough walls, while dry samples conceal water softening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b128-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「單軸強度與取樣」與「分類分項透明」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Uniaxial strength and sampling\" and \"Transparent classification components\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b128-v14-17","title":"單軸強度與取樣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Uniaxial strength and sampling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「單軸強度與取樣」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Uniaxial strength and sampling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單軸壓縮是完整岩石試件的強度，不包含大尺度節理。端面平整、長徑比與含水狀態影響破壞模式，若只挑完整段製樣，得到的分布會系統性排除最差地層。 假設直徑50 mm試體破壞荷重200 kN，σ=P/(πD²/4)=101.9 MPa；不等於岩體強度。 端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「單軸強度與取樣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniaxial compression measures intact specimen strength, excluding large joints. End preparation, slenderness and moisture influence failure. Selecting only pieces convenient for preparation systematically removes the weakest ground from the resulting distribution. An assumed 50 mm diameter specimen failing at 200 kN gives σ=P/(πD²/4)=101.9 MPa; this is not rock-mass strength. End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength. Applying that mean to the mass hides weak surfaces controlling deformation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Uniaxial strength and sampling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「單軸強度與取樣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Uniaxial strength and sampling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-17-k1","title":"單軸強度與取樣","titleEn":"Uniaxial strength and sampling","text":"單軸壓縮是完整岩石試件的強度，不包含大尺度節理。端面平整、長徑比與含水狀態影響破壞模式，若只挑完整段製樣，得到的分布會系統性排除最差地層。","textEn":"Uniaxial compression measures intact specimen strength, excluding large joints. End preparation, slenderness and moisture influence failure.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單軸強度與取樣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Uniaxial strength and sampling\" is correct?","options":["完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。","岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。","單軸壓縮是完整岩石試件的強度，不包含大尺度節理。"],"optionsEn":["Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass.","Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.","Uniaxial compression measures intact specimen strength, excluding large joints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單軸壓縮是完整岩石試件的強度，不包含大尺度節理。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniaxial compression measures intact specimen strength, excluding large joints. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b128-v14-18","title":"單軸強度與取樣：定量估算","titleEn":"Uniaxial strength and sampling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「單軸強度與取樣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Uniaxial strength and sampling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設直徑50 mm試體破壞荷重200 kN，σ=P/(πD²/4)=101.9 MPa；不等於岩體強度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 50 mm diameter specimen failing at 200 kN gives σ=P/(πD²/4)=101.9 MPa; this is not rock-mass strength. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測直徑與端面條件，拍攝破壞型態並追溯樣品孔號深度；把無法製樣的軟弱段另列，採相應試驗補足代表性，試驗主管依適用方法確認數據能否比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure diameter and end condition, photograph failure and trace hole-depth identity; list weak intervals that could not be prepared and investigate them appropriately, with the laboratory lead confirming method-compatible comparisons.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設直徑50 mm試體破壞荷重200 kN，σ=P/(πD²/4)=101.9 MPa；不等於岩體強度。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 50 mm diameter specimen failing at 200 kN gives σ=P/(πD²/4)=101.9 MPa; this is not rock-mass strength.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「單軸強度與取樣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Uniaxial strength and sampling\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。","折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor.","Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b128-v14-19","title":"單軸強度與取樣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Uniaxial strength and sampling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「單軸強度與取樣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Uniaxial strength and sampling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測直徑與端面條件，拍攝破壞型態並追溯樣品孔號深度；把無法製樣的軟弱段另列，採相應試驗補足代表性，試驗主管依適用方法確認數據能否比較。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure diameter and end condition, photograph failure and trace hole-depth identity; list weak intervals that could not be prepared and investigate them appropriately, with the laboratory lead confirming method-compatible comparisons. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength. Applying that mean to the mass hides weak surfaces controlling deformation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄單軸強度與取樣的資料來源與適用條件。量測直徑與端面條件，拍攝破壞型態並追溯樣品孔號深度；把無法製樣的軟弱段另列，採相應試驗補足代表性，試驗主管依適用方法確認數據能否比較。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for uniaxial strength and sampling. Measure diameter and end condition, photograph failure and trace hole-depth identity; list weak intervals that could not be prepared and investigate them appropriately, with the laboratory lead confirming method-compatible comparisons.","failure":"注意干擾：端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測直徑與端面條件，拍攝破壞型態並追溯樣品孔號深度；把無法製樣的軟弱段另列，採相應試驗補足代表性，試驗主管依適用方法確認數據能否比較。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。","textEn":"Measure diameter and end condition, photograph failure and trace hole-depth identity; list weak intervals that could not be prepared and investigate them appropriately, with the laboratory lead confirming method-compatible comparisons. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength. Applying that mean to the mass hides weak surfaces controlling deformation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄單軸強度與取樣的資料來源與適用條件。量測直徑與端面條件，拍攝破壞型態並追溯樣品孔號深度；把無法製樣的軟弱段另列，採相應試驗補足代表性，試驗主管依適用方法確認數據能否比較。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for uniaxial strength and sampling. Measure diameter and end condition, photograph failure and trace hole-depth identity; list weak intervals that could not be prepared and investigate them appropriately, with the laboratory lead confirming method-compatible comparisons.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「單軸強度與取樣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Uniaxial strength and sampling\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","量測直徑與端面條件，拍攝破壞型態並追溯樣品孔號深度；把無法製樣的軟弱段另列，採相應試驗補足代表性，試驗主管依適用方法確認數據能否比較。","岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure diameter and end condition, photograph failure and trace hole-depth identity.","High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測直徑與端面條件，拍攝破壞型態並追溯樣品孔號深度；把無法製樣的軟弱段另列，採相應試驗補足代表性，試驗主管依適用方法確認數據能否比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure diameter and end condition, photograph failure and trace hole-depth identity; list weak intervals that could not be prepared and investigate them appropriately, with the laboratory lead confirming method-compatible comparisons. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b128-v14-20","title":"單軸強度與取樣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Uniaxial strength and sampling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「單軸強度與取樣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Uniaxial strength and sampling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength. Applying that mean to the mass hides weak surfaces controlling deformation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Applying that mean to the mass hides weak surfaces controlling deformation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。","textEn":"End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength. Applying that mean to the mass hides weak surfaces controlling deformation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「單軸強度與取樣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Uniaxial strength and sampling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。","端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.","End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength."],"answer":2,"explanation":"端部摩擦可能使試件呈異常錐形破壞，缺陷樣本剔除過多又會抬高平均強度；將這種平均值直接給整體岩體，會掩蓋支配變形的弱面。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"End friction can produce abnormal conical failure, while rejecting too many flawed samples raises mean strength. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b128-v14-21","title":"分類分項透明：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transparent classification components: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「分類分項透明」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transparent classification components” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分類系統把多種觀測壓縮成工程指標，總分相同並不意味相同失效機制。強度佳但節理不利與強度弱但塊狀完整可能得到相似分數，設計必須保留各分項及地下水情境。 假設六個示範評分為12、15、10、20、7、−5，合計59；此加總練習不聲稱對應某版分類門檻。 把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分類分項透明」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Classification compresses observations into an index, but equal totals need not mean equal mechanisms. Strong rock with adverse joints can resemble weak but massive rock numerically, so component ratings and groundwater scenarios must remain visible. Assumed illustrative component scores of 12,15,10,20,7 and −5 total 59; this arithmetic exercise does not claim a threshold in a particular classification edition. Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness. Equal totals can then assign identical support to different mechanisms, overlooking wedge instability or squeezing ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transparent classification components” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分類分項透明」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transparent classification components”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-21-k1","title":"分類分項透明","titleEn":"Transparent classification components","text":"分類系統把多種觀測壓縮成工程指標，總分相同並不意味相同失效機制。強度佳但節理不利與強度弱但塊狀完整可能得到相似分數，設計必須保留各分項及地下水情境。","textEn":"Classification compresses observations into an index, but equal totals need not mean equal mechanisms. Strong rock with adverse joints can resemble weak but massive rock numerically, so component ratings and groundwater scenarios must remain visible.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分類分項透明」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transparent classification components\" is correct?","options":["分類系統把多種觀測壓縮成工程指標，總分相同並不意味相同失效機制。","岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。","乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。"],"optionsEn":["Classification compresses observations into an index, but equal totals need not mean equal mechanisms.","Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.","The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分類系統把多種觀測壓縮成工程指標，總分相同並不意味相同失效機制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Classification compresses observations into an index, but equal totals need not mean equal mechanisms. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b128-v14-22","title":"分類分項透明：定量估算","titleEn":"Transparent classification components: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分類分項透明」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transparent classification components” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設六個示範評分為12、15、10、20、7、−5，合計59；此加總練習不聲稱對應某版分類門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assumed illustrative component scores of 12,15,10,20,7 and −5 total 59; this arithmetic exercise does not claim a threshold in a particular classification edition. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存每一分項的原始依據、評分表版本及評分者，對地下水或取向做敏感度比較；以實際出露和變形驗證推薦支護的適用性，總分僅作索引而非自動施工指令。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain evidence, rating-table edition and assessor for every component and test water and orientation sensitivity; verify support applicability against exposures and movement, using the total as an index rather than an automatic construction instruction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設六個示範評分為12、15、10、20、7、−5，合計59；此加總練習不聲稱對應某版分類門檻。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assumed illustrative component scores of 12,15,10,20,7 and −5 total 59; this arithmetic exercise does not claim a threshold in a particular classification edition.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分類分項透明」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transparent classification components\", which statement holds?","options":["兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。"],"optionsEn":["Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b128-v14-23","title":"分類分項透明：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transparent classification components: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分類分項透明」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transparent classification components” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存每一分項的原始依據、評分表版本及評分者，對地下水或取向做敏感度比較；以實際出露和變形驗證推薦支護的適用性，總分僅作索引而非自動施工指令。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain evidence, rating-table edition and assessor for every component and test water and orientation sensitivity; verify support applicability against exposures and movement, using the total as an index rather than an automatic construction instruction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness. Equal totals can then assign identical support to different mechanisms, overlooking wedge instability or squeezing ground. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄分類分項透明的資料來源與適用條件。保存每一分項的原始依據、評分表版本及評分者，對地下水或取向做敏感度比較；以實際出露和變形驗證推薦支護的適用性，總分僅作索引而非自動施工指令。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for transparent classification components. Retain evidence, rating-table edition and assessor for every component and test water and orientation sensitivity; verify support applicability against exposures and movement, using the total as an index rather than an automatic construction instruction.","failure":"注意干擾：把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存每一分項的原始依據、評分表版本及評分者，對地下水或取向做敏感度比較；以實際出露和變形驗證推薦支護的適用性，總分僅作索引而非自動施工指令。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。","textEn":"Retain evidence, rating-table edition and assessor for every component and test water and orientation sensitivity; verify support applicability against exposures and movement, using the total as an index rather than an automatic construction instruction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness. Equal totals can then assign identical support to different mechanisms, overlooking wedge instability or squeezing ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄分類分項透明的資料來源與適用條件。保存每一分項的原始依據、評分表版本及評分者，對地下水或取向做敏感度比較；以實際出露和變形驗證推薦支護的適用性，總分僅作索引而非自動施工指令。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for transparent classification components. Retain evidence, rating-table edition and assessor for every component and test water and orientation sensitivity; verify support applicability against exposures and movement, using the total as an index rather than an automatic construction instruction.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分類分項透明」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transparent classification components\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。","保存每一分項的原始依據、評分表版本及評分者，對地下水或取向做敏感度比較；以實際出露和變形驗證推薦支護的適用性，總分僅作索引而非自動施工指令。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction.","Retain evidence, rating-table edition and assessor for every component and test water and orientation sensitivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保存每一分項的原始依據、評分表版本及評分者，對地下水或取向做敏感度比較；以實際出露和變形驗證推薦支護的適用性，總分僅作索引而非自動施工指令。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain evidence, rating-table edition and assessor for every component and test water and orientation sensitivity; verify support applicability against exposures and movement, using the total as an index rather than an automatic construction instruction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b128-v14-24","title":"分類分項透明：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transparent classification components: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分類分項透明」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transparent classification components” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness. Equal totals can then assign identical support to different mechanisms, overlooking wedge instability or squeezing ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equal totals can then assign identical support to different mechanisms, overlooking wedge instability or squeezing ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。","textEn":"Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness. Equal totals can then assign identical support to different mechanisms, overlooking wedge instability or squeezing ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分類分項透明」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transparent classification components\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。"],"optionsEn":["Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把缺少資料的分項設成最有利分數，會產生看似完整的分類；兩種機制不同的岩體因總分相同被配上同一支護，可能漏掉楔體或擠壓問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning favorable values to missing components creates false completeness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b128-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「乘法指標敏感」與「尺度與代表體積」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Multiplicative index sensitivity\" and \"Scale and representative volume\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b128-v14-25","title":"乘法指標敏感：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Multiplicative index sensitivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「乘法指標敏感」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Multiplicative index sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"乘法形式的岩體指標對分母與低值項特別敏感，輸入稍有改動即可跨越多個等級。這種指標是經驗模型，必須使用同一版本定義，不能把不同方法中同名因子混在一起。 假設Q=(60/9)(2/3)(1/5)=0.889；若Jw由1降為0.5，其餘不變，Q=0.444。 把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「乘法指標敏感」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multiplicative rock indices are sensitive to denominators and small factors, so modest input changes may cross several classes. These empirical models require consistent edition-specific definitions; similarly named factors from different systems are not interchangeable. For assumed Q=(60/9)(2/3)(1/5)=0.889, reducing Jw from 1 to 0.5 while holding other factors fixed gives Q=0.444. Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Multiplicative index sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「乘法指標敏感」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Multiplicative index sensitivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-25-k1","title":"乘法指標敏感","titleEn":"Multiplicative index sensitivity","text":"乘法形式的岩體指標對分母與低值項特別敏感，輸入稍有改動即可跨越多個等級。這種指標是經驗模型，必須使用同一版本定義，不能把不同方法中同名因子混在一起。","textEn":"Multiplicative rock indices are sensitive to denominators and small factors, so modest input changes may cross several classes. These empirical models require consistent edition-specific definitions; similarly named factors from different systems are not interchangeable.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「乘法指標敏感」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Multiplicative index sensitivity\" is correct?","options":["乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。","乘法形式的岩體指標對分母與低值項特別敏感，輸入稍有改動即可跨越多個等級。","岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。"],"optionsEn":["The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction.","Multiplicative rock indices are sensitive to denominators and small factors, so modest input changes may cross several classes.","The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor."],"answer":1,"explanation":"乘法形式的岩體指標對分母與低值項特別敏感，輸入稍有改動即可跨越多個等級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multiplicative rock indices are sensitive to denominators and small factors, so modest input changes may cross several classes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b128-v14-26","title":"乘法指標敏感：定量估算","titleEn":"Multiplicative index sensitivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「乘法指標敏感」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Multiplicative index sensitivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Q=(60/9)(2/3)(1/5)=0.889；若Jw由1降為0.5，其餘不變，Q=0.444。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed Q=(60/9)(2/3)(1/5)=0.889, reducing Jw from 1 to 0.5 while holding other factors fixed gives Q=0.444. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由原始節理組數、粗糙狀況、水情與應力描述追查各比值，另以合理上下限重算；若輸入只是假設，結果不得轉成精確支護間距，需由岩工工程師結合失效分析審查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace each ratio to joint-set count, surface condition, water and stress descriptions and recalculate plausible bounds; assumed inputs must not become precise support spacing without rock-engineering review of failure mechanisms.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Q=(60/9)(2/3)(1/5)=0.889；若Jw由1降為0.5，其餘不變，Q=0.444。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed Q=(60/9)(2/3)(1/5)=0.889, reducing Jw from 1 to 0.5 while holding other factors fixed gives Q=0.444.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「乘法指標敏感」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Multiplicative index sensitivity\", which statement holds?","options":["折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。","岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage.","High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b128-v14-27","title":"乘法指標敏感：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Multiplicative index sensitivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「乘法指標敏感」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Multiplicative index sensitivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由原始節理組數、粗糙狀況、水情與應力描述追查各比值，另以合理上下限重算；若輸入只是假設，結果不得轉成精確支護間距，需由岩工工程師結合失效分析審查。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace each ratio to joint-set count, surface condition, water and stress descriptions and recalculate plausible bounds; assumed inputs must not become precise support spacing without rock-engineering review of failure mechanisms. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄乘法指標敏感的資料來源與適用條件。由原始節理組數、粗糙狀況、水情與應力描述追查各比值，另以合理上下限重算；若輸入只是假設，結果不得轉成精確支護間距，需由岩工工程師結合失效分析審查。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for multiplicative index sensitivity. Trace each ratio to joint-set count, surface condition, water and stress descriptions and recalculate plausible bounds; assumed inputs must not become precise support spacing without rock-engineering review of failure mechanisms.","failure":"注意干擾：把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由原始節理組數、粗糙狀況、水情與應力描述追查各比值，另以合理上下限重算；若輸入只是假設，結果不得轉成精確支護間距，需由岩工工程師結合失效分析審查。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。","textEn":"Trace each ratio to joint-set count, surface condition, water and stress descriptions and recalculate plausible bounds; assumed inputs must not become precise support spacing without rock-engineering review of failure mechanisms. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄乘法指標敏感的資料來源與適用條件。由原始節理組數、粗糙狀況、水情與應力描述追查各比值，另以合理上下限重算；若輸入只是假設，結果不得轉成精確支護間距，需由岩工工程師結合失效分析審查。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for multiplicative index sensitivity. Trace each ratio to joint-set count, surface condition, water and stress descriptions and recalculate plausible bounds; assumed inputs must not become precise support spacing without rock-engineering review of failure mechanisms.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「乘法指標敏感」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Multiplicative index sensitivity\"?","options":["由原始節理組數、粗糙狀況、水情與應力描述追查各比值，另以合理上下限重算；若輸入只是假設，結果不得轉成精確支護間距，需由岩工工程師結合失效分析審查。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。"],"optionsEn":["Trace each ratio to joint-set count, surface condition, water and stress descriptions and recalculate plausible bounds.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"由原始節理組數、粗糙狀況、水情與應力描述追查各比值，另以合理上下限重算；若輸入只是假設，結果不得轉成精確支護間距，需由岩工工程師結合失效分析審查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace each ratio to joint-set count, surface condition, water and stress descriptions and recalculate plausible bounds; assumed inputs must not become precise support spacing without rock-engineering review of failure mechanisms. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b128-v14-28","title":"乘法指標敏感：失效診斷","titleEn":"Multiplicative index sensitivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「乘法指標敏感」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Multiplicative index sensitivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。","textEn":"Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「乘法指標敏感」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Multiplicative index sensitivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。","岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes.","The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把地下水因子視為永久不變會忽略季節或開挖導水，錯誤分母又可使指標偏差數倍；輸出小數位再多也不能補足取樣與判讀不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating water factors as permanent ignores seasonal or excavation-induced changes; an incorrect denominator shifts the index severalfold, and extra decimal places do not cure deficient sampling or interpretation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b128-v14-29","title":"尺度與代表體積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scale and representative volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「尺度與代表體積」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scale and representative volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"小岩心可能完全避開長而連續的節理，卻又把局部碎裂段過度放大。從厘米試件到隧道尺度需要描述結構面的持續性、間距與連通，不能只把試體尺寸比例套在強度上。 假設隧道直徑10 m、岩心直徑0.05 m，尺度比200；截面面積比200²=40000，不能據此直接縮減強度。 過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「尺度與代表體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Small cores may miss persistent joints while overemphasizing one crushed interval. Moving from centimetre specimens to tunnel scale requires persistence, spacing and connectivity, not a strength correction based solely on specimen dimensions. For assumed tunnel diameter 10 m and core diameter 0.05 m, length ratio is 200 and area ratio 40000; neither directly determines a strength reduction. Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scale and representative volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「尺度與代表體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scale and representative volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-29-k1","title":"尺度與代表體積","titleEn":"Scale and representative volume","text":"小岩心可能完全避開長而連續的節理，卻又把局部碎裂段過度放大。從厘米試件到隧道尺度需要描述結構面的持續性、間距與連通，不能只把試體尺寸比例套在強度上。","textEn":"Small cores may miss persistent joints while overemphasizing one crushed interval. Moving from centimetre specimens to tunnel scale requires persistence, spacing and connectivity, not a strength correction based solely on specimen dimensions.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「尺度與代表體積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scale and representative volume\" is correct?","options":["岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。","兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。","小岩心可能完全避開長而連續的節理，卻又把局部碎裂段過度放大。"],"optionsEn":["The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor.","Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias.","Small cores may miss persistent joints while overemphasizing one crushed interval."],"answer":2,"explanation":"小岩心可能完全避開長而連續的節理，卻又把局部碎裂段過度放大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Small cores may miss persistent joints while overemphasizing one crushed interval. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b128-v14-30","title":"尺度與代表體積：定量估算","titleEn":"Scale and representative volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「尺度與代表體積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scale and representative volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設隧道直徑10 m、岩心直徑0.05 m，尺度比200；截面面積比200²=40000，不能據此直接縮減強度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed tunnel diameter 10 m and core diameter 0.05 m, length ratio is 200 and area ratio 40000; neither directly determines a strength reduction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將岩心、露頭與掌子面節理圖放在共同坐標中，查核長節理是否延續及樣本是否覆蓋主要岩性；統計不收斂時須增補資料或給區間，不能以增加同一小區域樣本假裝提高全場代表性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate core, exposure and face-joint maps in one coordinate system, checking persistence and lithological coverage; nonconvergent statistics require added evidence or intervals, not merely more samples from the same small area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設隧道直徑10 m、岩心直徑0.05 m，尺度比200；截面面積比200²=40000，不能據此直接縮減強度。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed tunnel diameter 10 m and core diameter 0.05 m, length ratio is 200 and area ratio 40000; neither directly determines a strength reduction.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「尺度與代表體積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scale and representative volume\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。","不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run.","Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b128-v14-31","title":"尺度與代表體積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scale and representative volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「尺度與代表體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scale and representative volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將岩心、露頭與掌子面節理圖放在共同坐標中，查核長節理是否延續及樣本是否覆蓋主要岩性；統計不收斂時須增補資料或給區間，不能以增加同一小區域樣本假裝提高全場代表性。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate core, exposure and face-joint maps in one coordinate system, checking persistence and lithological coverage; nonconvergent statistics require added evidence or intervals, not merely more samples from the same small area. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄尺度與代表體積的資料來源與適用條件。將岩心、露頭與掌子面節理圖放在共同坐標中，查核長節理是否延續及樣本是否覆蓋主要岩性；統計不收斂時須增補資料或給區間，不能以增加同一小區域樣本假裝提高全場代表性。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for scale and representative volume. Integrate core, exposure and face-joint maps in one coordinate system, checking persistence and lithological coverage; nonconvergent statistics require added evidence or intervals, not merely more samples from the same small area.","failure":"注意干擾：過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將岩心、露頭與掌子面節理圖放在共同坐標中，查核長節理是否延續及樣本是否覆蓋主要岩性；統計不收斂時須增補資料或給區間，不能以增加同一小區域樣本假裝提高全場代表性。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。","textEn":"Integrate core, exposure and face-joint maps in one coordinate system, checking persistence and lithological coverage; nonconvergent statistics require added evidence or intervals, not merely more samples from the same small area. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄尺度與代表體積的資料來源與適用條件。將岩心、露頭與掌子面節理圖放在共同坐標中，查核長節理是否延續及樣本是否覆蓋主要岩性；統計不收斂時須增補資料或給區間，不能以增加同一小區域樣本假裝提高全場代表性。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for scale and representative volume. Integrate core, exposure and face-joint maps in one coordinate system, checking persistence and lithological coverage; nonconvergent statistics require added evidence or intervals, not merely more samples from the same small area.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「尺度與代表體積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scale and representative volume\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將岩心、露頭與掌子面節理圖放在共同坐標中，查核長節理是否延續及樣本是否覆蓋主要岩性；統計不收斂時須增補資料或給區間，不能以增加同一小區域樣本假裝提高全場代表性。","完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Integrate core, exposure and face-joint maps in one coordinate system, checking persistence and lithological coverage.","Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將岩心、露頭與掌子面節理圖放在共同坐標中，查核長節理是否延續及樣本是否覆蓋主要岩性；統計不收斂時須增補資料或給區間，不能以增加同一小區域樣本假裝提高全場代表性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate core, exposure and face-joint maps in one coordinate system, checking persistence and lithological coverage; nonconvergent statistics require added evidence or intervals, not merely more samples from the same small area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b128-v14-32","title":"尺度與代表體積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scale and representative volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「尺度與代表體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scale and representative volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩心與隧道的尺寸比可直接當成強度折減係數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The core-to-tunnel size ratio directly supplies the required strength-reduction factor.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。","textEn":"Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「尺度與代表體積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scale and representative volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。","過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias.","Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過度依賴完整小樣會低估大塊體滑落，單一破碎回次又可能使整段支護過度保守；兩種偏差都來自把局部觀測誤當代表體積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reliance on intact small samples underestimates large-block movement, whereas one crushed run may overstate support demand along a long reach; both mistakes confuse local evidence with a representative volume. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b128-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「記錄者差異控制」與「分類到模型交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Controlling logger differences\" and \"Classification-to-model handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b128-v14-33","title":"記錄者差異控制：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Controlling logger differences: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「記錄者差異控制」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Controlling logger differences” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岩心描述含觀察與判斷，顏色、風化與節理條件的用語須有共同基準。雙人記錄不是取平均即可，分歧若集中於某一因子，應先找照明、樣品狀態或定義差異。 假設20段中兩位記錄者有16段分類一致，原始一致率80%；它未扣除偶然一致，不能等同Kappa。 不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「記錄者差異控制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Core logging combines observation and judgment. Color, weathering and joint condition need common definitions. Independent logs should not simply be averaged; concentrated disagreement points to lighting, sample state or inconsistent definitions requiring review. If two loggers agree on 16 of an assumed 20 intervals, raw agreement is 80%; without chance correction this is not a kappa statistic. Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem. Designers then cannot distinguish changing ground from changing logging practice. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Controlling logger differences” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「記錄者差異控制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Controlling logger differences”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-33-k1","title":"記錄者差異控制","titleEn":"Controlling logger differences","text":"岩心描述含觀察與判斷，顏色、風化與節理條件的用語須有共同基準。雙人記錄不是取平均即可，分歧若集中於某一因子，應先找照明、樣品狀態或定義差異。","textEn":"Core logging combines observation and judgment. Color, weathering and joint condition need common definitions.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「記錄者差異控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Controlling logger differences\" is correct?","options":["岩心描述含觀察與判斷，顏色、風化與節理條件的用語須有共同基準。","兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。","折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。"],"optionsEn":["Core logging combines observation and judgment.","Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias.","Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岩心描述含觀察與判斷，顏色、風化與節理條件的用語須有共同基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Core logging combines observation and judgment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b128-v14-34","title":"記錄者差異控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Controlling logger differences: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「記錄者差異控制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Controlling logger differences” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設20段中兩位記錄者有16段分類一致，原始一致率80%；它未扣除偶然一致，不能等同Kappa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If two loggers agree on 16 of an assumed 20 intervals, raw agreement is 80%; without chance correction this is not a kappa statistic. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以盲重記固定比例岩心，交叉比較分項而非只比總分；用保留的照片和樣品討論分歧並記錄裁定依據，若方法改版則保留舊版，避免悄悄改寫原始觀察。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Blindly relog a fixed sample and compare components rather than totals; resolve discrepancies using retained images and specimens and document the basis, preserving earlier versions when methods change instead of rewriting original observations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設20段中兩位記錄者有16段分類一致，原始一致率80%；它未扣除偶然一致，不能等同Kappa。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If two loggers agree on 16 of an assumed 20 intervals, raw agreement is 80%; without chance correction this is not a kappa statistic.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「記錄者差異控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Controlling logger differences\", which statement holds?","options":["岩心回收率很高就代表岩石品質指標必定很高。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","洗乾淨的節理岩壁足以代表原位含填料剪切行為。"],"optionsEn":["High total core recovery necessarily means a high rock quality designation.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Cleaned joint walls adequately represent the original infilled joint's shear behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b128-v14-35","title":"記錄者差異控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Controlling logger differences: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「記錄者差異控制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Controlling logger differences” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以盲重記固定比例岩心，交叉比較分項而非只比總分；用保留的照片和樣品討論分歧並記錄裁定依據，若方法改版則保留舊版，避免悄悄改寫原始觀察。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Blindly relog a fixed sample and compare components rather than totals; resolve discrepancies using retained images and specimens and document the basis, preserving earlier versions when methods change instead of rewriting original observations. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem. Designers then cannot distinguish changing ground from changing logging practice. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄記錄者差異控制的資料來源與適用條件。以盲重記固定比例岩心，交叉比較分項而非只比總分；用保留的照片和樣品討論分歧並記錄裁定依據，若方法改版則保留舊版，避免悄悄改寫原始觀察。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for controlling logger differences. Blindly relog a fixed sample and compare components rather than totals; resolve discrepancies using retained images and specimens and document the basis, preserving earlier versions when methods change instead of rewriting original observations.","failure":"注意干擾：不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以盲重記固定比例岩心，交叉比較分項而非只比總分；用保留的照片和樣品討論分歧並記錄裁定依據，若方法改版則保留舊版，避免悄悄改寫原始觀察。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。","textEn":"Blindly relog a fixed sample and compare components rather than totals; resolve discrepancies using retained images and specimens and document the basis, preserving earlier versions when methods change instead of rewriting original observations. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem. Designers then cannot distinguish changing ground from changing logging practice.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄記錄者差異控制的資料來源與適用條件。以盲重記固定比例岩心，交叉比較分項而非只比總分；用保留的照片和樣品討論分歧並記錄裁定依據，若方法改版則保留舊版，避免悄悄改寫原始觀察。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for controlling logger differences. Blindly relog a fixed sample and compare components rather than totals; resolve discrepancies using retained images and specimens and document the basis, preserving earlier versions when methods change instead of rewriting original observations.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「記錄者差異控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Controlling logger differences\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","岩體分類總分相同，就表示它們具有相同破壞機制。","以盲重記固定比例岩心，交叉比較分項而非只比總分；用保留的照片和樣品討論分歧並記錄裁定依據，若方法改版則保留舊版，避免悄悄改寫原始觀察。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Equal rock-mass classification totals imply identical governing failure mechanisms.","Blindly relog a fixed sample and compare components rather than totals."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以盲重記固定比例岩心，交叉比較分項而非只比總分；用保留的照片和樣品討論分歧並記錄裁定依據，若方法改版則保留舊版，避免悄悄改寫原始觀察。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Blindly relog a fixed sample and compare components rather than totals; resolve discrepancies using retained images and specimens and document the basis, preserving earlier versions when methods change instead of rewriting original observations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b128-v14-36","title":"記錄者差異控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Controlling logger differences: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「記錄者差異控制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Controlling logger differences” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem. Designers then cannot distinguish changing ground from changing logging practice. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Designers then cannot distinguish changing ground from changing logging practice.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩位記錄者有分歧時，把總分平均就能消除偏差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Averaging two disagreeing loggers' total scores removes the underlying bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。","textEn":"Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem. Designers then cannot distinguish changing ground from changing logging practice.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「記錄者差異控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Controlling logger differences\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。"],"optionsEn":["Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同班次使用不同風化尺度會造成假的地質突變，總分平均反而藏住問題；後續設計無法知道變化來自地層還是記錄習慣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different weathering scales across shifts create artificial geological changes, and averaged totals hide the problem. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b128-v14-37","title":"分類到模型交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Classification-to-model handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「分類到模型交接」如何影響鑽孔岩心記錄與岩體分類的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Classification-to-model handover” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Core logging and rock-mass classification”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岩體分類提供經驗參考，數值模型還需要應力、構造與水文邊界。交接應列明哪些參數來自試驗、哪些來自關聯式，並說明不利節理是否顯式建模，避免同一弱化作用被重複計入。 假設10個設計參數中6個實測、4個推估，推估比例40%；這是證據組成而非模型失敗機率。 若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分類到模型交接」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Classification supplies empirical context while analysis also requires stress, structure and hydraulic boundaries. Handover distinguishes tested and correlated parameters and explicit joints, preventing the same weakening effect from being counted twice. If 6 of an assumed 10 design parameters are measured and 4 inferred, the inferred fraction is 40%; this describes evidence composition, not model failure probability. Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Classification-to-model handover” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分類到模型交接」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Classification-to-model handover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-37-k1","title":"分類到模型交接","titleEn":"Classification-to-model handover","text":"岩體分類提供經驗參考，數值模型還需要應力、構造與水文邊界。交接應列明哪些參數來自試驗、哪些來自關聯式，並說明不利節理是否顯式建模，避免同一弱化作用被重複計入。","textEn":"Classification supplies empirical context while analysis also requires stress, structure and hydraulic boundaries. Handover distinguishes tested and correlated parameters and explicit joints, preventing the same weakening effect from being counted twice.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分類到模型交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Classification-to-model handover\" is correct?","options":["折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。","岩體分類提供經驗參考，數值模型還需要應力、構造與水文邊界。","岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage.","Classification supplies empirical context while analysis also requires stress, structure and hydraulic boundaries.","Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run."],"answer":1,"explanation":"岩體分類提供經驗參考，數值模型還需要應力、構造與水文邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Classification supplies empirical context while analysis also requires stress, structure and hydraulic boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b128-v14-38","title":"分類到模型交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Classification-to-model handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分類到模型交接」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Classification-to-model handover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設10個設計參數中6個實測、4個推估，推估比例40%；這是證據組成而非模型失敗機率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If 6 of an assumed 10 design parameters are measured and 4 inferred, the inferred fraction is 40%; this describes evidence composition, not model failure probability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從設計參數表抽查至岩心箱、試驗單與分類公式，檢查單位、版本和尺度；針對推估參數安排敏感度包絡，只有主管工程師確認主控失效機制與資料相符後才釋出分析結論。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace model parameters to core boxes, test sheets and classification equations, checking units, edition and scale; bracket inferred values in sensitivity analysis and release conclusions only after engineering review of governing failure mechanisms.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設10個設計參數中6個實測、4個推估，推估比例40%；這是證據組成而非模型失敗機率。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If 6 of an assumed 10 design parameters are measured and 4 inferred, the inferred fraction is 40%; this describes evidence composition, not model failure probability.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分類到模型交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Classification-to-model handover\", which statement holds?","options":["不同方向鑽孔的表觀節理間距可以不修正直接比較。","完整岩心抗壓強度就是含節理岩體的設計強度。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Apparent joint spacing from differently oriented holes can be compared without correction.","Intact-core compressive strength is the design strength of the jointed rock mass.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b128-v14-39","title":"分類到模型交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Classification-to-model handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分類到模型交接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Classification-to-model handover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從設計參數表抽查至岩心箱、試驗單與分類公式，檢查單位、版本和尺度；針對推估參數安排敏感度包絡，只有主管工程師確認主控失效機制與資料相符後才釋出分析結論。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace model parameters to core boxes, test sheets and classification equations, checking units, edition and scale; bracket inferred values in sensitivity analysis and release conclusions only after engineering review of governing failure mechanisms. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄分類到模型交接的資料來源與適用條件。從設計參數表抽查至岩心箱、試驗單與分類公式，檢查單位、版本和尺度；針對推估參數安排敏感度包絡，只有主管工程師確認主控失效機制與資料相符後才釋出分析結論。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for classification-to-model handover. Trace model parameters to core boxes, test sheets and classification equations, checking units, edition and scale; bracket inferred values in sensitivity analysis and release conclusions only after engineering review of governing failure mechanisms.","failure":"注意干擾：若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從設計參數表抽查至岩心箱、試驗單與分類公式，檢查單位、版本和尺度；針對推估參數安排敏感度包絡，只有主管工程師確認主控失效機制與資料相符後才釋出分析結論。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。","textEn":"Trace model parameters to core boxes, test sheets and classification equations, checking units, edition and scale; bracket inferred values in sensitivity analysis and release conclusions only after engineering review of governing failure mechanisms. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄分類到模型交接的資料來源與適用條件。從設計參數表抽查至岩心箱、試驗單與分類公式，檢查單位、版本和尺度；針對推估參數安排敏感度包絡，只有主管工程師確認主控失效機制與資料相符後才釋出分析結論。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for classification-to-model handover. Trace model parameters to core boxes, test sheets and classification equations, checking units, edition and scale; bracket inferred values in sensitivity analysis and release conclusions only after engineering review of governing failure mechanisms.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分類到模型交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Classification-to-model handover\"?","options":["從設計參數表抽查至岩心箱、試驗單與分類公式，檢查單位、版本和尺度；針對推估參數安排敏感度包絡，只有主管工程師確認主控失效機制與資料相符後才釋出分析結論。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","乘法岩體指標中的地下水因子永遠不會隨施工改變。"],"optionsEn":["Trace model parameters to core boxes, test sheets and classification equations, checking units, edition and scale.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The water factor in a multiplicative rock index never changes during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從設計參數表抽查至岩心箱、試驗單與分類公式，檢查單位、版本和尺度；針對推估參數安排敏感度包絡，只有主管工程師確認主控失效機制與資料相符後才釋出分析結論。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace model parameters to core boxes, test sheets and classification equations, checking units, edition and scale; bracket inferred values in sensitivity analysis and release conclusions only after engineering review of governing failure mechanisms. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b128-v14-40","title":"分類到模型交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Classification-to-model handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b128-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分類到模型交接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Classification-to-model handover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「折減整體模數後再加同一節理弱化不會重複計算。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing bulk stiffness and adding the same joint weakening cannot double-count damage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b128-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。","textEn":"Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b128-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分類到模型交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Classification-to-model handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。","岩心缺失的深度可以任意放在該回次最底部。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening.","Missing core may always be assigned arbitrarily to the bottom of a run."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若同時折減整體模數又以低剛度節理表達同一裂隙，可能重複弱化；反過來省略節理而仍用完整岩模數，會得到不合理的小變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reducing bulk stiffness and adding soft joints for the same fractures can double-count weakening; omitting joints while retaining intact-rock stiffness produces unrealistically small movements in the opposite direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-geo3","v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
